MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The End of Heartache and The Oncoming Storm combine melodic passages with aggressive riffs, matching what I enjoy about In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "The War Within fits the fast, forceful riffing I enjoy in Advance And Vanquish, while Mezmerize appeals to the unusual rhythms and melodic shifts that draw me to Tool."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Blessed Hellride feels less suited to my mood because its bluesy groove does not give me the sharp, fast aggression I want today.",
    "Stone Sour and Lost and Found fit my broader listening interests, but they feel less urgent than the more intense metal choices; postponing them does not mean I dislike them."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A broadly heavy sound seems to count too much when the kind of riffing and balance of melody matter more to my choice.",
    "The connection between Damnation And A Day and Death Cult Armageddon makes sense, but symphonic heaviness alone does not make an album my next priority."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I am especially drawn right now to fast, precise riffs paired with memorable melodic hooks, rather than heaviness by itself.",
    "My recent interest in Tool makes rhythmic surprises appealing too, so an album can stand out through unusual shifts as well as sheer aggression."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You understood my interest in heavy music, but my strongest choices depend on sharp riffing, melodic hooks, and rhythmic interest rather than heaviness alone."
}
